# Copy to .env.local and point at your deployed Flask backend.
#
# IMPORTANT: the URL must include the `/api` prefix — every backend route
# is registered under `/api/*` (see backend/app.py). If you omit `/api`,
# the frontend will hit `/expenses` instead of `/api/expenses` and the
# browser will show a misleading "CORS error" that's actually a 404.
#
# Local dev default:
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
#
# Production example:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.expense.example.edu/api
#
# Notes on cross-origin (React on :5173, Flask on :5000):
# - Flask reads ALLOWED_ORIGINS from its env; leave it empty to fall back
#   to "*" (permissive, dev-only). In prod, set it to this frontend's URL.
# - S3 must ALSO have CORS configured on the receipts bucket, because the
#   browser PUTs receipt images directly to S3 via a presigned URL. See
#   localstack/init.py applies it to receipts-bucket automatically.
